<%# The DSFR card, written out rather than taken from `CardComponent`: that one
    puts the title in the heading it renders, where this card's heading is a
    wording the directories publish and wears their mark.

    The requirement names the card, and it is named whatever the directories
    answered afterwards — a requirement nobody serves is still one the procedure
    rests on. What stands under the rule is therefore what varies: the document
    and the button that asks for it, or the refusal that stands in for both.

    Everything is in the content, as the identity card has it, and the rule
    between the two halves is the `<hr>` that card draws: the DSFR footer pulls
    its own edge past the card's padding, so a rule on it would run wider than
    the wording above it. %>
<div class="<%= css_classes %>" id="<%= anchor %>" data-controller="demo-card">
  <%# The cross of an added card, in its top right corner. Its name is said in
      words to whoever cannot see the icon, which criterion 11.9 of the RGAA
      asks of a button whose label is one. Outside what an answer replaces, so
      no country chosen takes it away. %>
  <% if removable? %>
    <%= button_to removal_path, method: :delete, form: { class: 'requirement-card__remove', lang: 'en' },
          class: 'fr-btn fr-btn--tertiary-no-outline fr-btn--sm fr-icon-close-line',
          title: t('components.demo_requirement_card.remove') do %>
      <%= t('components.demo_requirement_card.remove') %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
  <div class="fr-card__body">
    <div class="fr-card__content">
      <%# The artwork the DSFR gives a document, at the height of the title and
          the line under it. Decorative: what it depicts is what the two lines
          beside it say. %>
      <div class="pictogram-row">
        <%= render PictogramComponent.new(name: 'document/document') %>

        <div class="pictogram-row__wording">
          <% if titled? %>
            <%# The requirement alone, and no sentence around it: the title is
                the directory's word and nothing of ours. %>
            <h3 class="fr-card__title fr-h5 fr-mb-1v">
              <%= render(DirectoryValueComponent.new(lang: requirement_language)) { requirement } %>
            </h3>
          <% end %>

          <%# The member state the evidence is to come from, above what it
              changes. Choosing sends it at once, and only what the resolution
              produces is replaced: the list keeps the focus, and the region
              below announces the new resolution — a content update, not the
              change of context RGAA 7.4 forbids. Offered on a card nothing
              satisfies too, which would otherwise have no way out of the
              country that serves nothing. %>
          <% if countries %>
            <%= form_with url: country_path, method: :patch, class: 'requirement-card__country fr-my-2w',
                  html: { lang: 'en' } do |form| %>
              <div class="fr-select-group fr-mb-0" data-demo-card-target="countryGroup">
                <%= form.label :pays, t('components.demo_requirement_card.country_label'),
                      class: 'fr-label', for: country_field %>
                <%= form.select :pays, options_for_select(countries, country_code), {},
                      class: 'fr-select', id: country_field,
                      data: { demo_card_target: 'countrySelect', action: 'change->demo-card#choose',
                              demo_card_list_param: 'country' } %>
                <%# What the card says when the choice got no answer this
                    application wrote: the server cannot say that it could not
                    be reached, so the sentence is rendered here, hidden, and
                    the controller shows it. Outside what an answer replaces,
                    so no answer takes it away but the controller. %>
                <%= tag.p t('components.demo_requirement_card.unreachable_html',
                            reload: link_to(t('components.demo_requirement_card.reload'),
                                            helpers.admin_demo_documents_path)),
                          class: 'fr-error-text', id: failure_field, hidden: true,
                          data: { demo_card_target: 'countryFailure' } %>
              </div>
              <%# The one region announcing what either list changed: it is never
                  replaced, by either answer. %>
              <p class="fr-sr-only" aria-live="polite" data-demo-card-target="status"></p>
            <% end %>
          <% end %>

          <%# What the country answers above the rule, which a country chosen
              replaces: the list of the combinations it publishes, where it
              publishes several — chapter 3.2.2 §2.3 has the user select one —;
              the country alone, in its box, on a card that follows a request
              and offers no list of countries; the sentence saying nothing
              satisfies the requirement there; or nothing. %>
          <div class="fr-card__desc" data-demo-card-target="top">
            <% if combinations %>
              <%# Choosing sends it at once, and only the foot of the card is
                  replaced: the list keeps the focus, and the region of the
                  form of countries — rendered whenever this list is —
                  announces what the foot now says. No combination is chosen in
                  the user's place, so the list opens on a prompt until one is. %>
              <%= form_with url: combination_path, method: :patch, class: 'requirement-card__evidence-type',
                    html: { lang: 'en' } do |form| %>
                <div class="fr-select-group fr-mb-0" data-demo-card-target="combinationGroup">
                  <%= form.label :combinaison, t('components.demo_requirement_card.combination_label'),
                        class: 'fr-label', for: combination_field, data: { demo_card_announced: true } %>
                  <%= form.select :combinaison, options_for_select(combinations, combination_id),
                        { prompt: (t('components.demo_requirement_card.combination_prompt') unless combination_id) },
                        class: 'fr-select', id: combination_field,
                        data: { demo_card_target: 'combinationSelect', action: 'change->demo-card#choose',
                                demo_card_list_param: 'combination' } %>
                  <%# Rendered here and hidden, as the country's: the server
                      cannot say it could not be reached. %>
                  <%= tag.p t('components.demo_requirement_card.combination_unreachable_html',
                              reload: link_to(t('components.demo_requirement_card.reload'),
                                              helpers.admin_demo_documents_path)),
                            class: 'fr-error-text', id: combination_failure_field, hidden: true,
                            data: { demo_card_target: 'combinationFailure' } %>
                </div>
              <% end %>
            <% elsif !countries %>
              <p class="fr-mb-0" lang="en" data-demo-card-announced><%= render country_tag %></p>
            <% elsif unsatisfiable? %>
              <p class="fr-mb-0" lang="en" data-demo-card-announced>
                <%= t('components.demo_requirement_card.unsatisfiable_html', country: render(country_tag)) %>
              </p>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <hr class="fr-mt-3w">

      <div class="requirement-card__actions" data-demo-card-target="foot">
        <%# One line per evidence type of the combination, in the order of the
            list: chapter 3.2.2 §2.3 has « at least one Evidence for each
            Evidence Type » provided, so each names its own provider, or says
            why it cannot. `data-demo-card-line` is what the answer to a line's
            questions finds that line by. %>
        <% lines.each do |line| %>
          <div class="requirement-card__line" data-demo-card-line="<%= line.evidence_type_uuid %>">
            <%# The questions the Data Service Directory asks on this line
                before it can name the provider, in the order its exception
                writes them, each labelled in its own language (RGAA 8.7) and in
                the control the DSFR gives its type. Answering sends them at
                once, as choosing a country or a combination does, once every
                question of the line has its answer; only the resolution of the
                line and the zone are replaced: the questions keep the focus
                and what was typed, and the region of the country form
                announces what the resolution now says (RGAA 7.4). %>
            <% if (asked = questions(line)) %>
              <%= form_with url: answer_path(line), method: :patch, class: 'requirement-card__questions',
                    html: { lang: 'en' }, data: { demo_card_target: 'questions', action: 'submit->demo-card#answer' } do %>
                <% answering = { action: 'change->demo-card#answer' } %>
                <% asked.each do |question| %>
                  <% label = render(DirectoryValueComponent.new(lang: question.language)) { question.label } %>
                  <% if question.control == :radio %>
                    <fieldset class="fr-fieldset fr-mb-2w" id="<%= question_field(line, question) %>" data-demo-card-question>
                      <legend class="fr-fieldset__legend fr-text--regular"><%= label %></legend>
                      <% { 'true' => 'yes', 'false' => 'no' }.each do |value, wording| %>
                        <div class="fr-fieldset__element fr-fieldset__element--inline">
                          <div class="fr-radio-group">
                            <%= radio_button_tag question_name(question), value, question.value == value,
                                  id: "#{question_field(line, question)}-#{value}", data: answering %>
                            <label class="fr-label" for="<%= question_field(line, question) %>-<%= value %>">
                              <%= t("components.demo_requirement_card.questions.#{wording}") %>
                            </label>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      <% end %>
                    </fieldset>
                  <% elsif question.control == :select %>
                    <%# The prompt is offered until a value is chosen, as the
                        list of the combinations offers its own. %>
                    <div class="fr-select-group fr-mb-2w" data-demo-card-question>
                      <label class="fr-label" for="<%= question_field(line, question) %>"><%= label %></label>
                      <%= select_tag question_name(question), options_for_select(question.options, question.value),
                            prompt: (t('components.demo_requirement_card.questions.prompt') unless question.value),
                            class: 'fr-select', id: question_field(line, question), data: answering %>
                    </div>
                  <% else %>
                    <div class="fr-input-group fr-mb-2w" data-demo-card-question>
                      <label class="fr-label" for="<%= question_field(line, question) %>"><%= label %></label>
                      <%= text_field_tag question_name(question), question.value, class: 'fr-input',
                            id: question_field(line, question), data: answering %>
                    </div>
                  <% end %>
                <% end %>
                <%# Rendered here and hidden, as the country's: the server
                    cannot say it could not be reached. Outside the resolution,
                    so no answer takes it away but the controller. %>
                <%= tag.p t('components.demo_requirement_card.questions.unreachable_html',
                            reload: link_to(t('components.demo_requirement_card.reload'),
                                            helpers.admin_demo_documents_path)),
                          class: 'fr-error-text fr-mb-2w', id: answer_failure_field(line), hidden: true,
                          data: { demo_card_target: 'answerFailure' } %>
              <% end %>
            <% end %>

            <div class="requirement-card__resolution" data-demo-card-target="resolution">
              <% if line.nameable? %>
                <p class="fr-mb-0" lang="en" data-demo-card-announced>
                  <%= t('components.demo_requirement_card.from_html',
                        evidence_type: render(DirectoryValueComponent.new(lang: line.evidence_type_language)) { line.evidence_type },
                        provider: render(DirectoryValueComponent.new(lang: line.provider_language)) { line.provider }) %>
                </p>

                <% if (version = unspoken(line)) %>
                  <%# A warning and not a sentence among others: the line names
                      a provider and the card offers nothing to ask it. The DSFR
                      alert carries its icon besides its colour, which RGAA 3.1
                      wants. %>
                  <div class="fr-alert fr-alert--warning fr-alert--sm fr-mt-2w requirement-card__refusal" lang="en">
                    <p><%= t('components.demo_requirement_card.unsupported_version', version: version.number) %></p>
                  </div>
                <% end %>
              <%# Questions still waiting for their first answers offer no
                  refusal: nothing is refused yet. %>
              <% elsif refused?(line) %>
                <%# Nothing to name is nothing to click: requirement 27 makes
                    the two names a condition of the request. What the
                    directories answered is said in the card's own words — the
                    code and the sentence they returned belong to the
                    operator's console, not to a portal — and a directory that
                    declined to answer is not a country publishing nothing, so
                    the line says which of the two happened. The sign says
                    again the warning the colour carries (RGAA 3.1), hidden
                    from the assistive technologies, which have the sentence. %>
                <p class="fr-mb-0 requirement-card__refusal" lang="en" data-demo-card-announced>
                  <span class="fr-mr-1v" aria-hidden="true">⚠️</span><%= refusal(line) %>
                </p>
              <% end %>
            </div>
          </div>
        <% end %>

        <%# A combination still to choose offers no button and no refusal:
            requirement 27 of chapter 1 §2 has the type and the provider named
            before any request is made, and nothing is refused yet. %>
        <% if refused_whole? %>
          <div class="requirement-card__resolution">
            <p class="fr-mb-0 requirement-card__refusal" lang="en" data-demo-card-announced>
              <span class="fr-mr-1v" aria-hidden="true">⚠️</span><%= refusal(wording) %>
            </p>
          </div>
        <% end %>

        <%# The buttons that open the exchanges, and everything that becomes of
            them, once every line names its provider: a combination is asked for
            whole. This element persists and its contents are what an answer
            replaces: it holds the announced region, which would announce
            nothing were it swapped out with what it announces. Its own
            wrapper is what an answer to a line's questions replaces, the zone
            appearing once the last line is resolved. %>
        <div class="requirement-card__request" data-demo-card-target="request">
          <% if askable? %>
            <div class="demo-request fr-mt-2w" aria-live="polite" data-controller="demo-request"
              data-action="submit->demo-request#submit"
              data-demo-request-url-value="<%= zone_path %>">
              <%= render zone %>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
